Local change to DPF (commit 4238e1c7f0351bbe488d79f0899c540543ac7583) for the macOS Audio Unit, ISC like the file it changes.
scripts/build-macos.sh applies it to a copy of DPF in build/macos/DPF; third_party/DPF stays exactly as cloned. It touches only the
AU wrapper, distrho/src/DistrhoPluginAU.cpp, which neither the Linux nor the VST3 build compiles.
DPF's AU wrapper does not publish parameter value names (its own TODO: "scale points to kAudioUnitParameterFlag_ValuesHaveStrings"),
so AU hosts would show position numbers (0 to 23) where the VST3 shows the panel legends (1 to 24, 1.2:1 / 2:1 / FLOOD, NICKEL / IRON / STEEL, ...).
This sets kAudioUnitParameterFlag_ValuesHaveStrings on parameters with enumeration values and answers
kAudioUnitProperty_ParameterValueStrings (indexed parameters), kAudioUnitProperty_ParameterStringFromValue and
kAudioUnitProperty_ParameterValueFromString from those values. It also notifies kAudioUnitProperty_Latency when a parameter change
alters the plugin's latency (DPF's AU wrapper lists that as a TODO), which QUALITY does.

